@1 = ~Hey, you! You are exactly what I was looking for! Mercenaries, am I right?~
@2 = ~Sort of. We eliminate problems, if that is what you mean.~
@3 = ~We take on jobs, providing the payment is satisfying.~
@4 = ~No. We are here to see the elephant so step aside.~
@5 = ~No, we're just travelers.~
@6 = ~Splendid. Exactly what I need. My name is Alfie and I am a mahout - an elephant trainer. This fine pal right here is Helios of Chult. I suppose you've never seen an elephant before.~
@7 = ~We are not made of gold per se but I am willing to provide a reward for your efforts. Few coins and a magical item if you're interested. My name is Alfie and I am a mahout - an elephant trainer. This fine pal right here is Helios of Chult. I suppose you've never seen an elephant before.~
@8 = ~Howdy, Alfie. What is it you need help with?~
@9 = ~How many coins are in play here?~
@10 = ~I think I will have to think about this first.~
@11 = ~You're back. I was hoping you'd be. Are you interested in my offer? Will you exterminate these filthy kobolds?~
@12 = ~I'll help you.~
@13 = ~Why can't you get Nashkel garrison involved?~
@14 = ~We won't work for you.~
@15 = ~It's about a group of kobolds that seem to be getting too close to the tents recently. As you probably noticed this part of the Carnival has a palisade erected to keep these things from us. They seem to come from eastern forests and whenever we chase them out, they keep rushing back within hours. Each time a guard takes business in their hands, little buggers take off into the woods. They are smart enough to know guards cannot leave the perimeter unprotected and therefore won't run after them. Kobolds look for opportunities to get in here and I believe I know the reason why.~
@16 = ~When Helios was performing balancing on small pedestals I spotted a few of them hiding behind the stands. I am still not sure how they evaded the guards but they gained access to this tent and I noticed that they were looking at Helios and he must've noticed them too, because he broke the act and started acting distressed. I managed to calm him down, people started realising something is wrong and I had to clear the tent prematurely and notify the guards.~
@17 = ~The next show was cancelled because I had to ensure Helios safety, as well as the audience's. Now, don't get me wrong. Helios could crush these pest in no time but I am not risking him getting hurt. I will require some help to get rid of them. And this is where you come in.~
@18 = ~I'll help you.~
@19 = ~Why can't you get Nashkel garrison involved?~
@20 = ~Why are all these chairs and tables so gigantic?~
@21 = ~We won't work for you.~
@22 = ~Awesome. Each group of kobolds was seen fleeing to the east, beyond the treeline. Sometimes they set up camps near the fence on the other side, sometimes deeper. Look around and try to locate any and do whatever it takes to ensure they vanish for good.~
@23 = ~I did speak to them. I was even granted an audience with Berrun Ghastkill himself but his hands are tied. Due to the crisis in the mines, his priorities lie elsewhere. He needs his soldiers in the mines at the moment, so I cannot count on his support. With condolences he granted me three guards, and sent a few to the main carnival but this isn't enough to track down these creatures.~
@24 = ~Practical reasons. The whole interior was designed specifically for Helios. All these items here are either for food preparation, harnessing, training, entertainment, some are simply for food storage or other equipment needed for elephant handling. The cage on the left isn't in use anymore. We used to have a lion from Anauroch but sadly he passed away from old age. So, all this is enlarged for many practical purposes. Besides, extra huge furniture is sensible for an elephant of that size, isn't it?~
@25 = ~Have you dealt with them?~
@26 = ~Yes. They will worry you no longer.~
@27 = ~Not yet.~
@28 = ~That's a weight off my shoulders. I am so grateful for your assistance. I shall uphold my end of the bargain. Here is 70 gold coins and a Scimitar. As promised. Take care.~
@29 = ~Helm almighty! So this is what they look like up close. Look at their beautiful trumpet. I always dreamed to see them up close.~
@30 = ~Magnificent creature! How dare they keep this glamorous being in this… cesspool of corruption and use it as... as attraction! This is vile, and only industrialization lovers support such barbaric approaches! I pressure us to leave this rotten hole. I can't look at the suffering of that creature.~
@31 = ~Boo and I have heard stories of such majestic animals but we've never seen any. It is… absolutely beautiful.~
@32 = ~How could this be? Such elegant creature… I never imagined it could look like this. My father used to share stories with me but to see one in real life is… astonishing.~
@33 = ~By the gods! Look at how huge he is. Now, this is something special compared to typical fauna of the Sword Coast.~
@34 = ~If there be any vista in these western lands worthy of our eyes since we departed Rashemen, it is assuredly this.~
@35 = ~I think I got the muse for my next ballad. 'Travelers of the Trumpet'.. ehm, I need to tweak that title.~
@36 = ~Phi, not as impressive as manticores back home. (although those tusks do look a fraction impressive)~
@37 = ~Can't say I enjoy the circus much, however this particular view is certainly noteworthy.~

@38 = ~Will you listen to my request?~
@39 = ~I can offer you seventy gold coins and a magical scimitar for your trouble. If that is enough to interest you, perhaps we can discuss the matter further.~
@40 = ~Seventy gold coins, along with the magical blade I mentioned. That is my offer. Will you hear the rest of my request?~
@41 = ~All right. Tell me what you need.~
@42 = ~I will have to think about this first.~
@43 = ~We already did defeat these kobolds. They were near the pond east from here.~

@50 = ~Alfie needs help dealing with a band of kobolds threatening his elephant and disrupting the Eastern Carnival. I agreed to look into the trouble near the ponds.~
@51 = ~The kobolds threatening Alfie and his elephant have been defeated. Alfie thanked us and rewarded our assistance.~

@52 = ~Thank you once again for saving me. Helios is most grateful.~
@53 = ~Woah. Puffguts used to tell me bedtime stories about elephants. They are exotic animals from across the world. I always dreamed of seeing them. Apparently, they live on Afyal island. Can we visit it one day?~
@54 = ~I don't want to make you any promises.~
@55 = ~Pretty pleaseeee. I promise it will be worth our while.~
